The SAM traffic follows the public SAMv3 specification through `truchman`, not
RNS's vendored i2plib:

- The I2P interface: HDLC over a SAM STREAM, a 1064-byte hardware MTU at the
  protocol link MTU, a 256 kbit/s bitrate guess and 16-byte default access
  codes; an empty-frame keepalive after 10 s without a write, the stream ended
  after 110 s without a read, redials every 15 s and session retries every 8 s
  (peer) or 15 s (listener); tunnel synthesis by the initiator only, under
  `I2PInterfacePeer[<name> to <peer>]`; peers that keep full mode and default
  policy while accepted streams inherit the section's settings. Unlike RNS,
  there is no "stale" state at 20 s (RNS only logs it), SAM is spoken directly
  rather than through forwarded local ports, and a failed write redials rather
  than tearing the interface down. RNS `Interfaces/I2PInterface.py` 323-331,
  337-441, 503, 507-533, 539-603, 719-720, 737, 805, 812-870.
  Targets: `src/endpoint/i2p.rs`, `src/endpoint/pump.rs`.
- The destination keyfile: `storagepath/i2p/<hex(H(H(name) + H(transport)))>.i2p`,
  the old `H(H(name))` file preferred when present, holding SAM's base64
  private key, generated with signature type 7 on first use. Unlike RNS, the
  file is created owner-only on unix. RNS `Interfaces/I2PInterface.py`
  229-252.
  Target: `src/endpoint/i2p.rs`.
- The `[[I2PInterface]]` section keys `peers` (a comma list) and
  `connectable`. RNS `Interfaces/I2PInterface.py` 728-735.
  Target: `src/endpoint/iface_config/carriers.rs`.

## Prns

Reference withdrawn September 26 over unresolved provenance concerns. Existing
attribution and license text remain for retained material; they do not verify
